flowchart TB
    accTitle: Save a credential draft
    accDescr: WinUI validates required editor fields, Presentation checks the current login, and Core validates and applies an add or update in memory. Core encrypts the entire vault and commits config and storage together. Failed persistence restores the in-memory mutation when the session still exists; cancelled drafts are discarded.
    draft["SECRET: editor draft\nPassword, optional TOTP and recovery codes"]:::secret
    draft --> choice{"Save or Cancel?"}
    choice -->|Cancel / confirm discard| discard["Discard draft\nExisting item stays unchanged"]
    choice -->|Save| ui{"Title, username, password\nand URL or No URL supplied?"}
    ui -->|Invalid| error["Show field errors\nKeep draft for correction"]:::danger
    ui -->|Valid| session{"Current login and\nauthorized vault access?"}
    session -->|No / cancelled / expired| reject["Reject action\nDiscard stale UI result"]:::danger
    session -->|Yes| core["Core: validate item, group,\nTOTP and unique recovery codes"]
    core -->|Invalid| error
    core -->|Valid| mutate["Add: new ID and timestamps\nUpdate: preserve ID, track password change"]
    mutate --> history["If password changed:\nkeep up to 10 previous passwords"]
    history --> encrypt["Encrypt whole VaultData with DEK\nAES-256-GCM + vault context"]
    encrypt --> commit[["Stage and commit .config + .storage\nSee storage-transaction diagram"]]
    commit -->|Success| saved["Refresh secret-free list\nReturn to Vault"]:::good
    commit -->|Failure| rollback["Undo in-memory mutation if still loaded\nReport error; do not claim success"]:::danger
    classDef secret fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#0f172a
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
    classDef good fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d
